oral bounds, maximal coupled Euler estimates, Bessel control and the terminal tail. Monotone gamma may have jumps; the proof uses its total variation, not its derivative. Constants need not remain bounded as T approaches one, and no effective numerical minimizer bounds or arbitrary prescribed diagonal rate are asserted. This rate is not a selected Lean conclusion.","citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-euler-normalization","scalar-r2-26-cite-correlation-vector-control","scalar-r2-26-cite-terminal-loss","support_regularity_source"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024","ordinary_deductions_review_20261026_r9"],"id":"scalar.fixed_strip_error_budget","kind":"claim","label":"Fixed-strip scalar accuracy with its cutoff dependence exposed","locator":"consequences.tex:124–196; long reasoning record §7.1, ordinary quantitative deduction","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-consequences","statement":"For each fixed admissible minimizer gamma and cutoff 0<T<1, finite constants C_(gamma,T), N0_(gamma,T) give |S_(T,N)-P_star|<=(1-T)m(T)+C_(gamma,T)sqrt(T/N) for N>=N0, where m(T)=E Phi_xx(T,X_T). The adjacent sum retains the rounding coordinate. Monotone quadrature costs at most Delta and weighted Gronwall uses exp(K_T integral_0^T gamma)<=exp(K_T).","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.fixed_strip_error_budget","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.fixed_strip_error_budget","id":"field:c7fa5083c234cd3d7bc3a635c0b702ababc7392f4d9e67dd70d9fa1279fb5a54","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.fixed_strip_error_budget","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"